# {{ project_name }}

Generated by Gurthang on Linux. The app follows a loco-shaped `src/` tree
with SQLx and Inertia. Database queries live in the sibling `models` crate.

## Setup

```bash
cp .env.example .env
npm install
gurthang db create
gurthang db migrate up
gurthang run
```

Open <http://127.0.0.1:3000>. `.env` includes `SQLX_OFFLINE=true`. Migrate and
generate/sync refresh `.sqlx` with `cargo sqlx prepare`. Host, port, session,
Inertia SSR, and worker settings live in `config/*.yaml`. `DATABASE_URL` stays
in env.

Release builds use Mold via `.cargo/config.toml`. Production:

```bash
gurthang build
APP_ENV=production target/release/{{ project_name }}
```

## Layout

- `models/` — `query!` / `query_as!`, factories
- `src/app.rs` — empty `App` implementing `Hooks`
- `src/controllers/` — each owns `routes()` via `mount!`
- `src/routes/` — named route catalog (name + path)
- `src/services/` — auth and workflows
- `src/workers/` — placeholder Postgres jobs
- `src/tasks/`, `src/mailers/`, `src/initializers/`
- `config/` — YAML per environment

## Growing the app

```bash
gurthang generate migration create_widgets
gurthang db migrate up
gurthang generate model Widget
gurthang generate scaffold Widget
gurthang generate job SendWelcome
gurthang sync routes
gurthang sync payloads
gurthang routes
```

`SQLX_OFFLINE=true cargo check` is the day-to-day compile. Edit a controller
without touching `models/` and the models crate stays cached.

## Jobs

```bash
cargo run
cargo run -- web
cargo run -- worker
```

```rust
use crate::workers::Job;

let job_id = ctx.jobs.enqueue(Job::PurgeExpiredSessions).await?;
```
